# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# True HTTP 301 for /github → framework repo (PRD §3 / §9). This takes
# precedence over the Astro-generated /github/index.html meta-refresh page,
# which stays as a fallback for any other host. Keep in sync with the
# `redirects` entry in astro.config.mjs.
/github  https://github.com/open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent  301

# Historical product URL still linked from third-party sites. Preserve its
# accumulated signals instead of leaving Search Console with a persistent 404.
/developer  /getting-started/quick-start/  301

# Conventional developer entry points. Agents (and people) probe /docs and
# /developers before they read a nav. /docs lands on the Getting Started index
# rather than a specific page, so the redirect stays right as that section grows.
# These live here rather than in astro.config.mjs `redirects` on purpose: the
# static build turns that config into a meta-refresh stub page, which a non-JS
# client sees as a 200 with no content — a real 301 is the whole point.
/docs        /getting-started/                301
/developers  /getting-started/quick-start/    301
